      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): bound AGENTS.md and prompt-input file reads with size cap",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nTwo file read paths in the session resource loader read files without any size bound, risking OOM from large or corrupted files:\n\n1. **`resolvePromptInput`** — reads user-supplied `--system-prompt` and `--append-system-prompt` files with unbounded `readFileSync`. A user could accidentally (or maliciously) point this at a multi-GB file, exhausting memory.\n\n2. **`loadContextFileFromDir`** — reads `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` project context files with unbounded `readFileSync`. These files are user-authored and can be arbitrarily large.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBoth paths use raw `fs.readFileSync` with no limit on file size. The fix adds a `readTextFileSafely` helper that:\n\n1. `statSync` the file first to check it is a regular file\n2. Rejects files exceeding the byte cap with a clear warning\n3. Only then reads content with `readFileSync`\n\nCaps:\n- **AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md context files**: 1 MiB — these are project metadata files, not meant to be large\n- **User-supplied prompt input files**: 10 MiB — these can include larger instructions but still capped\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Prevents OOM crashes from oversized input files during session startup\n- Preserves warning logs for non-regular-file paths (directories, devices)\n- Gracefully skips oversized files instead of crashing the process\n\n## Evidence\n\n**`pnpm test src/agents/sessions/resource-loader.test.ts`** — all 5 tests pass:\n\n- \"does not use unreadable prompt file paths as prompt content\" — existing test preserved\n- \"rejects oversized system prompt files\" — 11 MiB file rejected with warning\n- \"accepts system prompt files within the byte limit\" — normal file loads correctly\n- \"skips oversized AGENTS.md files during context file loading\" — 2 MiB AGENTS.md skipped\n- \"loads AGENTS.md files within the byte limit\" — normal AGENTS.md loads correctly\n\nTest output:\n```\n ✓ |agents| src/agents/sessions/resource-loader.test.ts (5 tests)\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  5 passed (5)\n```",
